-<!-- forge-claim:viz-vocabulary -->  <p><span class="k">viz.render</span> takes data and returns a chart specification. Thirteen chart types: <b>bar, line, area, scatter, heatmap</b> (from tabular rows; compiled to Vega-Lite, ECharts on request) and <b>treemap, sunburst, sankey, chord, force graph, choropleth, bubble map, flow map</b> (from node/link/geometry inputs; ECharts). Four input modes: a catalog pattern identity, explicit (chart type + encodings), suggest (rows only — the recommender picks), or a structured intent (goal, measures, dimensions). Pattern mode uses bundled authored data and presentation; unsupported interaction or layout is a typed authoring-only result (OODS-V167), and conflicting explicit operands return OODS-V166. The five Cartesian families return spec; the eight ECharts-primary families omit spec and return echartsSpec with output.echarts forced true and reason echarts-primary-family. Every successful result carries a content hash of the canonical spec; on request it also returns an accessible data table and a generated narrative derived from the same data. The 20 viz-category traits (marks, encodings, scales, layouts, interactions, scatter composition and geocoding) are the vocabulary the spec is normalised into.</p><!-- /forge-claim:viz-vocabulary -->
